.LONG TERM...(Saturday through next Wednesday)

The main concern is the short term.

A weekend cooling trend remains in the forecast. The strong ridge
over our forecast area will weaken. Dry weather is forecast.

&&

.AVIATION...(18Z TAFS)

VFR conditions are expected to continue as mid to high clouds
continue through the region. Light offshore flow will continue to
disrupt the marine layer today. These factors are both
contributing to the high confidence VFR forecast across the
terminals today. An afternoon sea breeze will easily overpower the
offshore gradient, with a moderate to fresh breeze expected in
the afternoon and evening. More consistent onshore flow is
expected to return by Thursday, bringing low clouds back into
play.

Vicinity of SFO...High confidence in VFR conditions through the TAF
period. Winds are currently light and variable, but the NW sea
breeze will take hold this afternoon. Gusty NW winds potentially
up to 15 kts could occur this afternoon.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR conditions are anticipated to
persist through the TAF period with mid to high clouds returning
overnight. Light drainage winds in the morning will flip to a
moderate onshore breeze in the afternoon.

